<%# The same places Comment#broadcast_to_thread puts a comment: under its parent
    when it is a reply, else at the end of the thread. A comment already on the
    page is replaced by its own copy (Turbo drops the duplicate by id). A reply
    only arrives under a comment already shown, so any arrival ends the empty
    state. %>
<%= turbo_stream.remove "comments_empty" if @comments.present? %>
<%= render partial: "post_catch_ups/missed_comment", collection: @comments, as: :comment %>
